  "files": [
    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  #pragma omp parallel\n  {\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n      // Force computation: each body's velocity update is independent.\n      #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        float fx = 0.0f;\n        float fy = 0.0f;\n        float fz = 0.0f;\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < nbodies; ++j) {\n          float dx = bodies[j].x - bodies[i].x;\n          float dy = bodies[j].y - bodies[i].y;\n          float dz = bodies[j].z - bodies[i].z;\n          float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n          float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n          float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n          fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n          fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n          fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n        }\n\n        bodies[i].vx += DT*fx;\n        bodies[i].vy += DT*fy;\n        bodies[i].vz += DT*fz;\n      } // implicit barrier before position update\n\n      // Position integration: independent per body.\n      #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\n        bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\n        bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\n      } // implicit barrier before next iteration\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n  free(bodies);\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using OpenMP worksharing constructs (#pragma omp for) with static scheduling inside a single parallel region reduces manual partitioning overhead and leverages compiler-optimized loop distribution, improving performance on 4 cores while preserving correctness.",
  "notes": "Replaced the manual contiguous chunking and explicit barriers with two #pragma omp for schedule(static) worksharing loops per iteration. The implicit barriers at the end of each worksharing construct provide the required synchronization between force computation and position update, and between iterations. Force computation is inlined to avoid repeated function calls.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Replace manual thread partitioning with #pragma omp for schedule(static) worksharing loops",
    "Remove explicit barriers (rely on implicit barriers of worksharing constructs)",
    "Inline force computation into the worksharing loop body"
  ]
